# L §5.14.1 Running reads (round 12): a binding over a decision's movements: "the decision declares the move or the
# kind in reads"; L §5.14.1 "A movement that reaches a running read ... of a place or a movement it doesn't declare
# ... is refused (LOAD-READS)": second binds over sweeps, which holds the decision first, and has no reads.
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input amt: money PLN
input dom: int
input late: int
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place savings: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
kind sweeps: transfers

move first[m in months]: sweeps
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  reads konto
  leg cash from konto to savings amount min(amt, bal(konto))

version plan_2026
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 1 000.00 PLN "own"
  dom = 5 "own"
  late = 28 "own"
  opening[konto] = 5 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[savings] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

move second[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  after first
  leg cash from konto to savings amount amt * count(x in sweeps on day_of(m, dom))

ask q: flows(second, 2026-01-01 .. 2026-01-31)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-READS ...
